s in 2017|Corridors in Landkreis Schw\u00e4bisch Hall|SRGB images|Featured pictures of objects in Germany|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation (49\u00b0 N, 9\u00b0 E)|Fire extinguishers in Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg|Minimalist photos of objects|Mahlm\u00fchle aus Weipertshofen (Freilandmuseum Wackershofen)|Photographs of Hohenloher Freilandmuseum by Aristeas|Minimalist photographs of Germany|Taken with Sony ILCE-7M2 and Sony FE 55mm F1.8 ZA","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"quality|featured|potd","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"49.134247","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"9.696139","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"A wall in the hallway of the historical <i>Mahlm\u00fchle</i> (gristmill) from Weipertshofen in the <i>Hohenlohe open-air museum</i> at Wackershofen near <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schw%C3%A4bisch_Hall\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Schw\u00e4bisch Hall\">Schw\u00e4bisch Hall</a>, Germany.<br>The hallway of the <i>Mahlm\u00fchle</i> from Weipertshofen is painted bright blue according to historical models. (According to the explanatory plaque on site, this blue wall paint was very popular at the end of the 19th century because affordable blue wall paints \u2013 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultramarine#19th_century_%E2%80%93_the_discovery_of_synthetic_ultramarine\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Ultramarine\">synthetic ultramarine</a> \u2013 were something completely new at the time). Here there is a charming colour contrast with the (modern) red fire extinguisher.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on\u00a04 August 2017, 15:46:49","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wiki